              "content": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "data": "Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**`src/classify.py`** — completely rewritten with:\n\n1. **`StratifiedKFold`** instead of `KFold` — uses a label-combination hashing approach where each unique multi-label vector gets a stratification ID. Rare combos (< 5 samples) are merged into a bucket to prevent SKF errors.\n\n2. **`get_fold_indices(dataset, n_splits, random_state)`** — generates fold indices once from the raw dataset. You call this once and pass the same `folds` list to BERT, SVM, and baseline to guarantee identical data splits.\n\n3. **`crossValidate(model_or_name, train_dataset, model_type, ...)`** — the main function:\n   - `model_type=\"bert\"` → uses `Trainer.predict()` on each fold\n   - `model_type=\"svm\"` → TF-IDF + `OneVsRestClassifier(LinearSVC)`\n   - `model_type=\"baseline\"` → TF-IDF + `DummyClassifier(most_frequent)`\n\n4. **Comprehensive metrics** via `compute_full_metrics()`:\n   - Overall: accuracy, f1-micro, f1-macro, precision-micro, precision-macro, recall-micro, recall-macro\n   - Per-class: f1, precision, recall, support for each of the 12 classes\n\n5. **Output**: fold-level CSV (`{model}_cv.csv`), per-class CSV (`{model}_per_class.csv`), and `info.json` updated with `cv_results`.\n\n6. **`fineTune()`** kept as a backward-compatible wrapper — now returns `(modelc, results)`.\n\n**`main.py`** — updated to:\n- Generate folds once with `classify.get_fold_indices(train)` \n- Pass them to BERT fine-tuning and to SVM/Baseline cross-validation\n- All models evaluate on the exact same data splits"
